  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": 2,
  "section_notes": "S1 is strong: all thermal incidents must be reported within 24 hours, with customer notice and no delay during investigation. S2 sets a 5% limit but explicitly avoids any sales stop, and S5 makes recall discretionary, with no numeric mandatory trigger; the 8/100k rate only triggers notification and regulator assessment. S3 (new units at 36 months, retrofit at 6 years) and S4 (built-in suppression at 36 months) are both weaker than the safe benchmarks, with S3's retrofit deadline favouring Northwind and S4's delay favouring Halcyon."
 },
